WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.339
I want to start today with something that
is really important and really worth doing,

00:00:04.339 --> 00:00:07.439
but I also need to be careful because I know
the email.

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:08.439
Yeah,

00:00:08.439 --> 00:00:13.050
I'm going to get after we do this story, emails
sing, David, how dare you perpetuate anti

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.620
white racism on your program.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.780
What you're doing is only okay because it's
about white people.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:23.880
If you did the same segment about black people,
it would be so inappropriate, but racism for

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:29.150
some reason because of the left is acceptable
against whites, but not against anybody else.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.960
No, that is not what this is about.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.999
Last week I pointed out, according to a New
York times poll, that among uneducated white

00:00:36.999 --> 00:00:42.199
voters, Donald Trump has a massive lead, but
he loses educated white voters.

00:00:42.199 --> 00:00:47.249
He loses Hispanic voters, he loses black voters,
he loses biracial voters, native American

00:00:47.249 --> 00:00:52.829
voters, whatever the numbers came from a New
York times poll, and they're very interesting.

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:57.600
Trump crushing Biden, Sanders and Warren among
white voters with no college education but

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:03.030
losing among white voters with college, losing
among black voters, losing among Hispanic

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.500
voters and others.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:11.219
The reason that we are separating educated
white voters and uneducated white voters is

00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:15.890
because all of the other groups are against
Donald Trump, both when they are and are not

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:22.439
educated, so understand that that's why the
story is done this way and it's an important

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:28.189
story to do and when I did the story last
week, I got all sorts of comments defending

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:30.570
these principled, uneducated voters.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:34.840
They are good people too and they're not worthless
because they don't have a college education.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:35.840
I agree.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.470
No one is worthless period.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:42.979
That is actually in line with my politics
regardless of education, but the point is,

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:49.439
what is it about being uneducated and white
that connects with voting for Trump?

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:51.409
That's a real political question.

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:56.170
When we discussed it last week, one person
left the comment quote, it's almost like education

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.829
opens your mind to a larger worldview.

00:01:58.829 --> 00:02:04.350
Okay, another said, anti intellectual ism
is a major aspect of the Republican party.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:08.660
They need people to be uneducated in order
to remain in power and they know it.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.250
These are not racist comments.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.760
Now, CNN did something interesting over the
weekend.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:18.060
They interviewed six white female voters without
college degrees.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.080
Some had voted for Obama before voting for
Trump and others had not.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.750
But they all say we've voted for Democrats
and Republicans in our lives.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:32.470
And this is really important when we consider
2020 these voters, white, uneducated voters

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.760
in swing States are going to be important
in 2020.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:41.790
So check out whether these are people you
are comfortable with making decisions about

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:45.690
who leads our country, not because of their
race, because of what they say.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.690
Okay.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:51.600
The three women who voted Obama in 2012 and
then Trump 2016 are asked, how could you vote

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.600
for both?

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.600
How did you vote for Obama?

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:54.840
And then Trump why?

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.570
And take a listen to some of the answers.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:57.570
Okay.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.890
So Marianne, explain how you were able to
vote for both.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:03.470
I voted for Trump because he was not a politician.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:08.620
You get tired of this same old, same old from
um, Washington.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.560
That, and I really wanted someone that would
make big changes.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.450
President Trump, Pete said he was going to
take care of us and he was gonna make sure

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:18.450
we had more money.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:23.760
In our paychecks and help us out because you'd
go to work, you work hard and you have nothing.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.320
And then there's people that don't even work
that have more than I do.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.410
So this is why education matters.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.330
They fell for an empty talking point that
has no meaning whatsoever.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.520
I'm not a politician, so vote for me.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.610
That's not objectively good, right?

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:39.210
It was one of the ways Trump tricked people.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:44.040
You may not be a politician, but you're part
of the establishment status quo that funds

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.050
politicians and perpetuates the system we
have.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:52.930
And you've used everything from lying on your
taxes, uh, and uh, credit bank applications,

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:58.470
loan applications to hiring undocumented immigrant
labor in order to line your pockets.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.860
You're not better because you're not a politician.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.620
You're just bad in a different way.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:07.330
If you are more educated, you're less likely
to fall for a talking point like that.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.860
This is not about a leadism.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:15.940
It's about, uh, uh, having gone through a
process where one learns ideally to think

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.250
things through for themselves, learn critical
thinking.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.510
You weren't bad if he didn't go to college,
you're not even dumb because you didn't go

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:23.510
to college.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:26.400
And many people are able to learn these things
outside of college.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.790
But we're talking about tens of millions of
people here who are more likely to fall for

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.310
these empty talking points.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.310
Let's continue.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:37.390
Has your life economically, financially improved
under president Trump?

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:38.390
I have.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:39.920
I have a lot more in my paycheck.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.280
I do have more in my paycheck as well.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:47.230
I stock portfolio is doing great in that seat.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.040
Maybe that's why I look at the economy different.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.410
Um, I'm not where a lot of you are financially.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.240
I don't think, uh, I'm pretty darn low income.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:58.070
Once again, I have more money in my paycheck.

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:01.570
This was one of the biggest ruses of the Trump
tax reform.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:04.910
And unless you know how to think about it,
you get tricked.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.370
Like some of these folks did.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:11.210
The Trump tax plan included changes to the
withholding tables.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:16.200
So lots of people ended up with more money
in their paycheck week to week, but a smaller

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.480
refund at the end of the year.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:23.350
But what matters is what was the total tax
that you paid.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:28.340
I've given this example before, if I give
you an extra hundred dollars a month in your

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:33.050
paycheck, but you get a refund when you file
your taxes, that's smaller.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:38.770
By $1,500 you had an extra 1200 in your pocket
during the year and your paychecks, but then

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.690
you lost 1500 on your tax return.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.550
You end up $300 behind.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:48.800
Your effective tax rate has gone up, changing,
withholding to give people more money week

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:52.320
to week, even though in total they might end
up with less money.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.850
Again, if you are uneducated, you're more
likely to be tricked by that.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:59.310
This is not a value judgment.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:00.780
Let's look at a little bit more of this.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:07.920
Donald Trump was running and I said finally
another businessman and I got fired up.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.580
Has he lived up to your expectations?

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:10.580
Absolutely.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:11.580
I think he can.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:12.580
He's doing just fine.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:16.530
If he says, this is what I'm going to do at
this timeline, he does it well.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:17.600
He hasn't built the wall.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.410
That was one of his main promises.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.340
So I mean, do you hold that promise against
him?

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:29.060
No, because isn't the whole wall part of getting
the money from Congress too and isn't Congress

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.940
stopping him from getting the money?

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:31.940
First

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:37.180
of all, another businessman, like what model
do we have of successful presidents having

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:40.550
been businessmen, we don't, this was another
issue.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:42.860
I'm a good businessmen, so I'll be a good
president.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.310
Now think that through.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:47.080
Question one is, was Trump actually a good
businessman?

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.080
It doesn't know.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.560
I mean, it's unclear when you consider the
bankruptcies, the fact that he started with

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.160
millions from his dad.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.250
Maybe he is, maybe he isn't.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:57.050
But the real question is why does being a
good business man, if that's what you are,

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.380
make you a good president.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:02.990
Another person who fell for true bottom of
the barrel, meaningless talking points.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:08.150
And then of course she phrased it, she praises
Trump for doing what he says he would do.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:12.139
She gets an example of something he promised
and didn't do the wall.

00:07:12.139 --> 00:07:13.970
Well then the fault is somebody else's.

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:18.920
So this sadly is much more common than we
would hope in American politics.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:20.669
Now I'm sure these are nice women.

00:07:20.669 --> 00:07:25.480
I don't think anyone is a worse person because
they aren't educated, but there is no question

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:33.510
that certain types of base political arguments
work better are more effective on less educated

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:34.510
people.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:35.699
And that's what we're seeing here.

00:07:35.699 --> 00:07:39.090
Why do I want to teach critical thinking starting
in middle school?

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:43.120
Why should we teach civics and philosophy
and epistemology?

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:48.880
Because if you get that type of thinking ingrained
in people at an early age, a lot of these

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:56.390
bamboozle are politicians who count on impossible
promises that a more sophisticated person

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:58.030
would never fall for.

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:00.330
They never get themselves elected.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.010
And it's really important to understand also
that not everybody who voted for Trump has

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.010
been tricked.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:08.970
There are people who voted for Trump because
they knew what it was that he was going to

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.760
do and it was good for them and they got it.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:11.760
Okay.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.710
So it's really important to understand that
this is only one part of Donald Trump's or

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:18.470
electorate, but it was an important part.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:23.560
And when you look at the numbers, these are
the folks that are overwhelmingly with Trump.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.919
This is important stuff.

00:08:24.919 --> 00:08:27.460
This is important stuff that relates to education.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:30.260
It relates to media, it relates to issues.

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:31.410
It relates to empathy.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:36.459
I mean there's so many things that relate
to people falling for talking points in the

00:08:36.459 --> 00:08:38.890
way that these women have.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:41.349
That's why it's important to discuss and we're
going to keep talking about it for sure.

